  "type": "feature",
  "title": "PR mode in the app: make the Pull requests tab live",
  "stage": "monitor",
  "status": "complete",
  "spec": "The 'Pull requests' tab in the served repo page is a dead decorative span. PR mode exists only as a CLI command writing a standalone file, so a person using the app cannot reach it. Wire it: list a repo's open PRs from the tab, tour one on click, with the same background-job + building-page treatment repo tours already get. Acceptance: (1) the tab is live when the repo has a GitHub remote and inert with an honest reason when it does not; (2) it lists open PRs with title, number, author and branch; (3) clicking one builds and serves its tour without leaving the app; (4) a build in progress shows the existing building page, not a hang; (5) a repo with no checkpoint says so and links to the digest action rather than silently starting one; (6) no new external requests in the served page.",
